In modern ABAP (7.40 and later), while you cannot directly use SELECT ... INTO to fill 
a SELECT-OPTIONS table (range table) due to the incompatible structure, you can achieve the same result
succinctly using Inline Declarations and the VALUE or FOR operators.
Example 1: 
*& Report ZST67_FILL_SEL_0PT
*&---------------------------------------------------------------------*
*&
*&---------------------------------------------------------------------*
REPORT ZST67_FILL_SEL_0PT.

data lg_matnr type matnr.

SELECT-OPTIONS ls_matnr FOR lg_matnr.

at selection-screen OUTPUT.

SELECT 'I' AS sign, 'EQ' AS option, matnr AS low
  FROM mara
  INTO TABLE @ls_matnr .


Example 2:
SELECT 'I' AS sign, 'EQ' AS option, matnr AS low
  FROM mara
  INTO TABLE @DATA(lt_range) .
